mesa/kosmickrisp: work under virglrenderer Venus on macOS.
Venus there backs every host-visible allocation, and every shareable image, with shared memory
imported as host memory: a MTLBuffer that holds buffers and linear textures only.
- A GPU-only memory type, which tiled images always use (host image copy of tiled images goes
  through the texture, so it needs no host-visible memory).
- Linear color attachments (single-layer 2D textures, never promoted to arrays for input
  attachments): shareable render targets, which compositors draw into, are linear.

